// Title: Uncommon File Creation By Mysql Daemon Process
// Sigma ID: c61daa90-3c1e-4f18-af62-8f288b5c9aaf
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Joseph Kamau
// Date: 2024-05-27 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: stealth
// Description: Detects the creation of files with scripting or executable extensions by Mysql daemon. Which
//   could be an indicator of "User Defined Functions" abuse to download malware.
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://asec.ahnlab.com/en/58878/
//   - https://www.levelblue.com/blogs/spiderlabs-blog/honeypot-recon-mysql-malware-infection-via-user-defined-functions-udf/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/cb982537eb7397f93785ec066cce7b017050a43f/rules/windows/file/file_event/file_event_win_mysqld_uncommon_file_creation.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceFileEvents
| where (InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "\\mysqld.exe" or InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "\\mysqld-nt.exe") and (FolderPath endswith ".bat" or FolderPath endswith ".dat" or FolderPath endswith ".dll" or FolderPath endswith ".exe" or FolderPath endswith ".ps1" or FolderPath endswith ".psm1" or FolderPath endswith ".vbe" or FolderPath endswith ".vbs")
